            <ArticleTitle>Superior vena cava obstruction and dissecting aortic aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A dissecting aneurysm of the aorta led to formation of a fistula from the aneurysmal sac to the left atrium and caused obstruction of the superior vena cava. We do not know of any previous reports of this clinical syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
